  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Le livret signalétique",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Le livret signalétique\"**\n\nEvery stable gets a livret, like the identity booklet a horse carries: numbered fields, true data, an official stamp once it is complete. The system is a near-white page ruled by hairlines, inked in a green-black, set in a single grotesk with character, where prices are the loudest information and two colours (Vert, Rose casaque) make all the noise. Precision in the layout, humour in the words.\n\nDensity is editorial and calm: generous page margins (88px), large square photographs, a field grid of 1px hairlines that carries structure instead of cards and shadows. Vert owns whole regions (a poster, a price card, a brand tile, the primary button); Rose casaque is a highlighter band under one key word and the fill of the flot stamp. The flot de concours is a precise geometric stamp earned by a listing, never a costume.\n\nThe world refuses the directory default: grey cards, star ratings, a map as the hero. The price comes first, and it is set like a record, in tabular digits.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-white paper, green-black ink, 1px lilac-grey hairlines.",
      "Two loud colours only, used as regions and highlights, never as scattered accents.",
      "One family (Bricolage Grotesque) from 11px labels to 192px wordmark, driven by the width axis.",
      "Numbered field labels structure every livret.",
      "The flot: an 18-scallop rosette stamp that a listing earns field by field.",
      "Square-cornered photography; 6px radius on UI only."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Loud Colours Rule",
        "body": "On a typical page the proportions are paper 66 %, ink 16 %, vert 12 %, rose 6 %. Vert and Rose occupy whole zones or a single highlighted word; everything else stays quiet.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rose Legibility Rule",
